    IDS_MSG_URL_HTTPS                "This URL uses an encrypted connection (HTTPS)."
    IDS_MSG_TLS_MISSING              "This action needs HTTPS support, but libeay32.dll / ssleay32.dll are missing from the program folder. Please put them next to LocalSendXP.exe."
    IDS_SET_HTTPS                    "Enable HTTPS encryption(&E)"
    IDS_SET_LEGACY                   "Allow TLS 1.0/1.1 fallback for old devices(&L)"
    IDS_SET_INSECURE                 "Allow insecure HTTPS, no certificate check(&I)"
    IDS_SET_CLIENTCERT               "Require a client certificate(&R)"
    IDS_GRP_SECURITY                 "HTTPS / TLS encryption"
    IDS_STATUS_HTTPS                 "HTTPS"
    IDS_ABOUT_TLS_OFF                "HTTPS is not enabled (missing libeay32.dll / ssleay32.dll, or disabled in Settings)"
    IDS_MSG_TLS_NOFINGERPRINT        "The peer announces HTTPS but provides no certificate fingerprint, so it cannot be verified. Please search for devices again."
    IDS_MSG_HTTPS_DISABLED           "The peer uses HTTPS, but HTTPS is disabled on this computer. Please enable HTTPS encryption in Settings and try again."
    IDS_HELP_TITLE                   "Help"
    IDS_HELP_TEXT                    "1. Sending files\r\nSelect a receiver in the nearby devices list, then choose File > Send file, or simply drop the files onto the main window.\r\n\r\n2. Sending a folder\r\nSelect a receiver, then choose File > Send folder; every file inside that folder is sent to the peer.\r\n\r\n3. Receiving files\r\nWhen the peer starts a transfer a confirmation window appears. Tick the files you want to keep and press Accept; they are saved to the receive folder configured in Settings.\r\n\r\n4. Receiving from a URL\r\nChoose File > Receive from URL, paste the URL shared by the peer, then press OK.\r\n\r\n5. Sharing through a browser\r\nChoose File > Share via browser, pick the files, then copy the generated URL; the peer can download them with a web browser.\r\n\r\n6. Refreshing devices\r\nPress F5, or choose Device > Refresh devices, to search the local network again.\r\n\r\n7. Settings\r\nTools > Settings changes the device name and model, the listening port, the receive PIN, the save folder, the system tray and the auto-start options.\r\n\r\n8. HTTPS encryption\r\nEnable HTTPS in Tools > Settings > Security. A certificate is generated automatically and its fingerprint is shown on the settings page so that both sides can compare it. An encrypted connection is used only when both sides have HTTPS enabled.\r\n\r\n9. Receive history\r\nTools > History (Ctrl+H) lists the files that have been received. Double click a record to show it in Explorer; records can be deleted or cleared without touching the files on disk."
    IDS_ABOUT_TITLE                  "About LocalSend XP"
